data: {"type":"done","reply":"For a bright pop lead with sibilance issues, I'll put corrective EQ first to tame any harsh build-up, then a dedicated de-essing stage from TDR Nova in dynamic mode, compression to keep the vocal planted up front, a touch of harmonic excitement for presence, and a short verb last to place it in the room.\n\nNote: no dedicated pitch correction or delay plugin is in your available list — if you want transparent tuning, add one manually before the chain. TDR Nova is doing double duty here (corrective EQ in slot 1, dynamic de-essing in slot 2), which is a legitimate use of its multiband dynamics.\n\n<<<ECHOJAY_CHAIN>>>{\"chain\":[{\"name\":\"TDR Nova\",\"role\":\"Corrective EQ\",\"settings\":\"High-pass around 100Hz to clear low-end clutter; small cut 2–3dB around 250–300Hz if boxy; broad 1–2dB dip around 8–10kHz to take the edge off before de-essing\",\"settings_structured\":{\"low_cut_freq_hz\":100}},{\"name\":\"TDR Nova\",\"role\":\"Dynamic de-esser\",\"settings\":\"Set a dynamic band centred around 7–9kHz, threshold pulled down until 3–5dB of reduction triggers on the loudest esses only; keep the band narrow (high Q) so surrounding air isn't touched\"},{\"name\":\"Kotelnikov\",\"role\":\"Compression\",\"settings\":\"Medium attack around 10–15ms to let transients through, release around 80ms, aim for 4–6dB of gain reduction on the loudest phrases; this keeps the vocal forward and consistent\",\"settings_structured\":{\"attack_ms\":12,\"release_ms\":80}},{\"name\":\"La Petite Excite\",\"role\":\"Harmonic excitement / presence\",\"settings\":\"Light high-frequency excitation, mix low — adds the sheen a bright pop vocal needs without pushing sibilance back up\",\"settings_structured\":{\"mix_pct\":20}},{\"name\":\"Valhalla VintageVerb\",\"role\":\"Reverb\",\"settings\":\"Room or small plate, decay around 1.2s, wet around 10% — short enough to keep the vocal upfront\",\"settings_structured\":{\"reverb_decay_s\":1.2,\"wet_pct\":10}}],\"explanation\":\"Corrective EQ and dynamic de-essing handle the sibilance before compression locks in the forward, consistent level. Exciter after dynamics adds presence without re-energising the esses. Reverb last, kept short and low so nothing pushes the vocal back.\",\"result\":\"Chain built — two TDR Nova instances into Kotelnikov, La Petite Excite, and Valhalla VintageVerb.\"}<<<END_CHAIN>>>","modelName":"Oracle 2.7","resolvedTurnType":"chain_generate","stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"in":4517,"out":643,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":0.023196,"chainBlock":"ok"}

